course: dictionary
lesson: 8915
title: Many meanings of sickness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Sickness is a good example. It can mean being ill, a particular illness, or feeling like you might throw up. To work out which meaning fits, read the words around it. Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Real illness doesn't come and go to match homework and play, so fake sickness shows a pattern.» Here sickness means being ill. Fake sickness means pretending to be ill. The clue is the word fake, which tells you the person is not really ill.
explain: «When you are tired and thirsty on a walk, tell your grown-up, rest and drink water, because exhaustion leads to falls and heat sickness.» Heat sickness is a particular illness. The word a shows that it is one named illness, and the walk and the heat tell you what causes it.
fact: Sickness means being ill or unwell.
fact: A sickness is a particular illness or disease. Its plural is sicknesses.
fact: Sickness can also mean feeling like you are going to vomit (throw up), as in «travel sickness» or «seasickness».
fact: A «sickness bug» is a mild illness that spreads from person to person, and washing hands helps stop sickness spreading.
exercise: «Washing your hands helps stop sickness spreading.» What does sickness mean here? | *An illness caused by germs | A long holiday | A loud noise | A sunny afternoon at the park
exercise: Lily feels queasy on the boat and says she has seasickness. What does seasickness mean? | A kind of fish | A sunny day by the sea | A fear of swimming in the sea | *Feeling like you might be sick because of the waves
exercise: What is a sickness bug? | A tiny insect that bites | A kind of sandwich | A dance move | *A mild illness that spreads quickly
test: Sickness is uncountable, but a sickness has a plural. Which is the plural of a sickness? | *sicknesses | sicknesss | sickness | sickneses
test: «Real illness doesn't come and go to match homework and play, so fake sickness shows a pattern.» What does fake sickness mean? | Real germs in the air | A happy holiday | A long walk in the rain | *Pretending to be ill
exam: When you are tired and thirsty on a walk, what can lead to heat sickness? | Eating too many sweets | Reading a long book | *Being hot and tired without enough water | A cold swim in a lake
